'Toy-curve run of the production rho procedure in trails (escapes to 2*canon(M), cscore.rho_sigma.Walk). Input (JSON on stdin): curve: "a3" (y^2 = x^3 - 3x + b, negation classes, key = Montgomery x; P-256 shape); bits (of p), trials, adder_bits, dp_bits, walks, seed, tau_e4 (budget tau * 10^4), adder_key_shift (adders redrawn until (p >> shift) >> 39 <= key < p >> shift; 0 = uniform adders); escape: "double" (the only mode; escape to 2*canon(M)). Every trial samples a uniform secret and runs the procedure to its end at the budget: trails from fresh coins with no coefficient tracking while walking; each slot restarts at every distinguished point, takes L steps, then finishes its current trail; the first key match replays both trails from their coins; a degenerate match fails. It reports the success rate against 1 - exp(-tau). Toy scale only: tests the procedure and its collision statistics, not production cost.\n'
import json
import random
import sys
from cscore import groups, rho_sigma, rho_trails

def main():
 cfg = json.load(sys.stdin)
 for k, v in rho_trails.DEFAULTS.items():
  cfg.setdefault(k, v)
 cfg.setdefault('curve', 'a3')
 if cfg.setdefault('escape', 'double') != 'double':
  raise SystemExit('escape must be "double"')
 rng = random.Random(cfg['seed'])
 if cfg['curve'] == 'a3':
  E, G, n = groups.find_prime_order_curve(cfg['bits'], rng)
  cls = rho_sigma.NegationX(E.p, n)
  curve = {'p': E.p, 'a': E.a, 'b': E.b, 'order': n}
 else:
  raise SystemExit('curve must be a3')
 out = {'curve': curve, 'config': cfg}
 out.update(rho_trails.run(E, G, n, cls, cfg, rng))
 out['scope'] = 'toy curves only; runs the production procedure including resolution, not production cost'
 print(json.dumps(out))
if __name__ == '__main__':
 main()
